window.DM_BENCHP={"meta":{"last":"2026-11-10","n_all":1256,"built":"2026-11-11","note":"Outside figures are quoted from their publishers and kept apart from Dream Menu data. They measure different things (polls of all adults, delivery orders, menus, sales), so a difference is a finding, not an error."},"items":[{"id":"pineapple","topic":"Pineapple on pizza","theme":"Debates","tier":"public","verdict":"agrees","kind":"level","dm":{"v":49.3,"unit":"%","text":"49.3% say yes","base":"1,230 guests"},"ext":{"v":53,"unit":"%","text":"53% of Britons like pineapple on pizza","who":"YouGov, GB adults","date":"2017","url":"https://yougov.co.uk/news/2017/03/06/does-pineapple-belong-pizza"},"extra":"A January 2024 YouGov survey again found that more than half of Britons love or like it (reported by Reuters, January 2025).","read":"Foodies split almost exactly like the general public. Pineapple is a genuine 50:50 call, so it belongs on a pizza menu as an option, not a statement."},{"id":"tea","topic":"Tea or coffee","theme":"Debates","tier":"public","verdict":"differs","kind":"level","dm":{"v":67.4,"unit":"%","text":"67.4% pick coffee (25.4% tea)","base":"957 guests"},"ext":{"v":37,"unit":"%","text":"Among under-35s, 37% prefer coffee and 25% prefer tea","who":"YouGov polling, reported by Beverage Daily","date":"July 2025","url":"https://www.beveragedaily.com/Article/2025/07/01/delifrance-brews-up-fresh-insight-into-the-uks-coffee-craze/"},"extra":"Across all British adults, 41% drink tea and 40% drink coffee at least twice a day (YouGov Profiles, 2025). In 2012, 52% of Britons preferred tea.","read":"Even against younger Britons, the most coffee-led group in national polling, Dream Menu guests lean much further to coffee. That reflects who answers (urban, food-led, many in the trade), so read coffee demand here as the leading edge, not the national average."},{"id":"irnbru","topic":"Irn-Bru or Coke","theme":"Debates","tier":"public","verdict":"differs","kind":"level","dm":{"v":46.1,"unit":"%","text":"46.1% pick Irn-Bru (33.4% Coke)","base":"1,229 guests"},"ext":{"v":21,"unit":"%","text":"Irn-Bru was 21% of 330ml cans sold with Scottish takeaways, against 36% for Coke","who":"Scoffable takeaway orders, Scotland","date":"2022","url":"https://www.scoffable.com/article/irnbru-vs-coke-ten-years-of-takeaway-data"},"extra":"AG Barr says Irn-Bru accounts for one in every two flavoured fizzy drink cans in Scotland and grew ahead of the soft-drinks market (Circana, 12 weeks to 18 July 2026).","read":"Irn-Bru wins the loyalty question; Coke wins the order that comes with a takeaway meal. Both are true: one is identity, the other is habit. A range in Scotland needs both, with Irn-Bru as the local signal."},{"id":"water","topic":"Tap water with dinner","theme":"Debates","tier":"public","verdict":"agrees","kind":"level","dm":{"v":34.7,"unit":"%","text":"34.7% ask for tap water","base":"1,230 guests"},"ext":{"v":33,"unit":"%","text":"About a third of people drink tap water when eating out in restaurants","who":"Local Government Association survey, 3,000 people","date":"2016","url":"https://www.yorkshirepost.co.uk/health/tap-water-should-be-offered-families-eating-out-1799806"},"read":"Roughly one diner in three takes tap water in both sources. The rest split between still and sparkling, so a bottled water offer still matters to two tables in three."},{"id":"matcha","topic":"Matcha","theme":"Trends","tier":"public","verdict":"differs","kind":"direction","dm":{"dir":"down","text":"The trend guests most want binned, named by 9.2% of all interviews","base":"1,256 interviews"},"ext":{"dir":"up","text":"Consumers choosing matcha lattes 33.5% more than a year earlier; matcha dishes on UK menus doubled","who":"Tastewise, UK consumer and menu data","date":"June 2026","url":"https://tastewise.io/blog/uk-menu-trends"},"extra":"A matcha iced latte was one of the UK’s top trending Deliveroo orders of 2025.","read":"Growth and backlash at once: the classic sign of a polarising trend near its peak. Serve it well for the fans who want it, but don’t build a menu identity around it."},{"id":"pistachio","topic":"Dubai chocolate and pistachio","theme":"Trends","tier":"public","verdict":"differs","kind":"direction","dm":{"dir":"down","text":"Second most-named trend to bin, named by 8.4% of all interviews","base":"1,256 interviews"},"ext":{"dir":"up","text":"Pistachio reaching consumers 44% faster than a year earlier; pistachio with chocolate up 28%","who":"Tastewise, UK consumer data","date":"June 2026","url":"https://tastewise.io/blog/uk-menu-trends"},"read":"The same pattern as matcha. Pistachio as a flavour still has room; the viral Dubai bar format is what foodies are tired of."},{"id":"loaded","topic":"Loaded and dirty food","theme":"Trends","tier":"public","verdict":"differs","kind":"direction","dm":{"dir":"down","text":"3.0% of all interviews name loaded and dirty food as a trend to bin","base":"1,256 interviews"},"ext":{"dir":"up","text":"Loaded fries and shareable potato platters recommended as plant-forward wins for pubs and bars","who":"UKHospitality trend report","date":"2026","url":"https://www.ukhospitality.org.uk/?p=10357"},"read":"A gap between what the trade is advised to add and what foodies say they are tired of. Worth testing before adding loaded formats to a menu."},{"id":"tiramisu","topic":"Tiramisu","theme":"Dishes","tier":"public","verdict":"agrees","kind":"direction","dm":{"dir":"flat","text":"Steady staple: 12.2% of dessert answers, between 10.3% and 14.5% in every full quarter","base":"dessert answers"},"ext":{"dir":"up","text":"Tiramisu up nearly 15% in consumer demand","who":"Tastewise, UK consumer data","date":"June 2026","url":"https://tastewise.io/blog/uk-menu-trends"},"read":"The biggest single dessert on the Dream Menu, and still growing in the wider market. As safe as dessert gets."},{"id":"ooh","topic":"How often Scotland eats out","theme":"Market","tier":"public","verdict":"context","kind":"context","dm":{"text":"Dream Menu asks what people would choose, not how often they buy","base":"1,256 interviews"},"ext":{"text":"Out-of-home transactions in Scotland fell 7% in 2025, to 809 million; delivery transactions fell 30%","who":"Food Standards Scotland, Worldpanel by Numerator","date":"2026","url":"https://www.foodstandards.gov.scot/science-and-evidence/monitoring-out-of-home-food-and-drink-purchases-in-scotland-and-great-britain-2024-2025"},"read":"Fewer trips make each visit count for more. Dream Menu shows what people want from the visits they still make: the dishes worth leaving the house for."},{"id":"sites","topic":"Venues trading","theme":"Market","tier":"public","verdict":"context","kind":"context","dm":{"text":"Guests have named 1,935 venues","base":"venue mentions"},"ext":{"text":"Britain had 98,319 licensed venues in September 2026, 977 fewer than a year earlier (−1.0%)","who":"NIQ Hospitality Market Monitor (CGA data)","date":"October 2026","url":"https://www.vinetur.com/en/20261030110108/britain-lost-977-licensed-hospitality-venues-in-the-year-to-september.html"},"read":"A shrinking market concentrates demand. The venues guests name repeatedly are the ones with a reason to visit that survives a squeeze."}]};
